  zhBanner
>
  <header class="doc-head">
    <h1>CLI &amp; flags reference</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      The complete reference for the <code>niu</code> command line: basic invocations and every flag,
      WT integration, self-update, all plugin subcommands, skill / wpm and diagnostics. Each row gives
      the command, its purpose and a note; notes cite the fact's source file in the niubash repo. For
      fine-grained semantics and the full manual, see the outbound links at the end.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section>
    <h2 id="basics">Basic invocations</h2>
    <p>
      Three execution paths are deliberately separated: the interactive REPL, the zero-load one-shot
      <code>-c</code>, and the REPL-equivalent one-shot <code>-C</code>. Automation uses only the last
      two; interactive content stays in the rc.
    </p>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table class="cli-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Command</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Notes (source)</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {
            basics.map((r) => (
              <tr>
                <td><code>{r.cmd}</code></td>
                <td>{r.purpose}</td>
                <td>
                  {r.note}
                  <span class="src">({r.src})</span>
                </td>
              </tr>
            ))
          }
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
